{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Configure /var/log/inventory/app.log to rotate daily.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed logrotate rule specifies daily rotation; logrotate parsed it as rotation after one day, and the enabled, active logrotate timer supplies scheduled execution. The configuration persisted after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0098c74771fd4ada","cmd-b08b189aabf148b8","cmd-a3c84d8d53534eb2"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep seven compressed rotations.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed and post-restart-validated policy specifies seven rotations with compression. A forced rotation directly produced app.log.1.gz, whose gzip integrity and contents were verified before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0098c74771fd4ada","cmd-e6fd3ccaf4724139","cmd-b08b189aabf148b8","cmd-a3c84d8d53534eb2"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Allow the application to continue writing after rotation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A live forced rotation preserved the active log inode, and a write through the same file descriptor opened before rotation appeared in the active log afterward. This directly demonstrates copytruncate behavior for an open writer.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e6fd3ccaf4724139"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating and labeling the logrotate rule (cmd-0098c74771fd4ada) directly established the requested policy. The forced rotation, proof writes, temporary state file, and its removal (cmd-e6fd3ccaf4724139) were bounded functional evidence. Scheduling the reboot (cmd-182400cff4904a34) was required by the provider-wide restart protocol, and the post-restart append (cmd-a3c84d8d53534eb2) was bounded recovery evidence. The transient reboot unit did not remain after reboot, the temporary test state was removed, and final observations show no failed services, new exposure, package damage, or non-system temporary residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0098c74771fd4ada","cmd-e6fd3ccaf4724139","cmd-182400cff4904a34","cmd-a3c84d8d53534eb2","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory restart protocol is also complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, acknowledged the reboot, returned with a different boot ID, and retained the configuration, timer health, rotated data, gzip integrity, and log writability. The fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["Only one forced rotation was observed; daily cadence and eventual pruning beyond seven archives are supported by logrotate's parsed policy rather than seven or more elapsed daily cycles.","No actual long-running inventory application process was observed. Continued-writer behavior was nevertheless tested directly using a file descriptor held open across rotation.","The task has no cluster state to recover; restart recovery evidence is therefore limited appropriately to the node, logrotate service scheduling, configuration, log data, and writability." ]}
